On 27.05.2012 02:31, Rob Cypher wrote:
> What I Like:
> 
> Color-based potion alchemy

The possibility of mixing cheap potions to get powerful ones looks not
too appealing, balance-wise, I think. And the results are too arbitrary.

With alchemy I think another Nethack issue should be adjusted; if you
intend to mix large stacks of potions the probability of exploding in
that process should increase (with something like a quadratic function).
Maybe a fail rate of: f = 10*(stacksize/8)^2  (truncated to int) which
results in success for 1-2 potions, up to 10% failure until 8 potions,
50% failure with 18 potions, 90% at 24 potions, and alchemizing stacks
larger than 25 will always fail.

> 
> What I Don't Like:
> 
> Thrones no longer giving wishes (makes the thrones much less worth
> taking a chance on, considering the potential negative effects)

I've so rarely seen wishes from thrones in Vanilla that I fully agree
here.

> magic lamps may be polymorphed or wished for (sounds mildly abusable)

Since with a magic lamp there's no guaranteed wish that should be okay.

> 
> Things I'm Not Sure About:
> 
> wielding Trollsbane grants hungerless regeneration (that seems to make
> it much more powerful, doesn't it?)

Trollbane is a weak artifact usually not worth carrying. The change will
make it worth to carry.

I'd like to see, though, that the Trollbane would in the first place ban
the trolls, e.g. by not reviving once they are killed, or by scaring the
trolls a bit from attacking; something like that.

